From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 05:49:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: Implement DirectComposition devices, with visuals
 other processes compose into.

WebView2 hosts its content "window to visual" when Office asks it to,
as for the dialog of Word's Upgrade button: the host process shares a
visual of its tree through a private interface of the device, hands
the handle to the browser process, and that opens it as a target and
puts its own window in it, a transparent pop-up kept where the visual
is on the screen, through which input falls to the host's window.
With no device at all, the dialog closed as soon as it opened.

The devices of the DirectComposition API (IDCompositionDevice) now
keep trees of visuals with their offsets, transforms, clips, effects
and content, the transforms, clips and effect groups, and targets for
windows, two at most per window as the documentation says, one above
its children and one below them, whatever API made them.

Wine composes no window into another, so the window shown in a shared
visual is shown instead of being drawn there: made visible and still
letting input through, and owned by the top-level window of the
target, which keeps it above it.  Either process does this when it
commits, since either may be the last.  Nothing else of the trees is
drawn yet; surfaces and animations are not implemented.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

